{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 3873464,
  "courseSlug": "nextjs-react-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Next.js & React - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "41159736",
      "title": "Handling Errors",
      "lectureOrder": 111,
      "videoOrder": 104,
      "sourceHash": "8a59c56b87ea091d4c6dfb883eb4656e6a9a923032163b697814214bc26779e5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.33,
          "end": 2.58,
          "en": "Now this loading.JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.58,
          "end": 5.1,
          "en": "even though we're not using it anymore here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.1,
          "end": 8.46,
          "en": "is not the only other special file you can add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.46,
          "end": 11.76,
          "en": "in that app folder in your next project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.76,
          "end": 14.88,
          "en": "because besides loading and page and layout,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.88,
          "end": 18.843,
          "en": "we, for example, can also add an error.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.77,
          "end": 23.58,
          "en": "which will handle potential errors that might be generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.58,
          "end": 25.86,
          "en": "by your pages and components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.86,
          "end": 29.43,
          "en": "for example, if loading some data fails,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.43,
          "end": 32.94,
          "en": "and that of course could happen here if our database",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.94,
          "end": 37.23,
          "en": "is offline, which is unlikely for a SQLite database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.23,
          "end": 38.44,
          "en": "but which could happen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.402,
          "end": 40.98,
          "en": "if it would be a remote database server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.98,
          "end": 43.203,
          "en": "or if anything else goes wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.1,
          "end": 48.71,
          "en": "And to simulate this, let's simply go to the lib folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.71,
          "end": 52.02,
          "en": "in the meals.js file and then here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.02,
          "end": 55.35,
          "en": "let's throw an error, a new error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.35,
          "end": 57.843,
          "en": "where we say loading meals failed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.01,
          "end": 61.35,
          "en": "Something like this, doesn't really matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.35,
          "end": 63.03,
          "en": "Now if I do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 63.03,
          "end": 66.36,
          "en": "and I remove this error.js file again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.36,
          "end": 67.56,
          "en": "We'll re-add it soon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.56,
          "end": 70.05,
          "en": "but if I remove it for now, you'll see that now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 70.05,
          "end": 73.28999999999999,
          "en": "if we reload this page, we'll load the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.28999999999999,
          "end": 75.18,
          "en": "and after five seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.18,
          "end": 76.35300000000001,
          "en": "we'll get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.25,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "And the error screen we see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 83.373,
          "en": "is just a development version of this error screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.737,
          "end": 86.67,
          "en": "In production, this would look differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.67,
          "end": 89.22,
          "en": "We see this screen during development",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.22,
          "end": 92.46000000000001,
          "en": "so that it's easier for us as a developer to find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.46000000000001,
          "end": 93.723,
          "en": "and fix the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.56,
          "end": 96.87299999999999,
          "en": "In production, this would look differently.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.95,
          "end": 100.11,
          "en": "Now therefore, it's a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.11,
          "end": 103.95,
          "en": "to also add some error handling to your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.95,
          "end": 107.7,
          "en": "And you can do that by adding an error.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.7,
          "end": 110.46000000000001,
          "en": "And in that file, you then set up a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 110.46000000000001,
          "end": 115.46000000000001,
          "en": "that will be rendered by NextJS whenever an error occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 118.71000000000001,
          "en": "Though, it'll only handle errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 118.71000000000001,
          "end": 122.13,
          "en": "that occur in the page that sits in the same folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.13,
          "end": 126.483,
          "en": "as this error.js file or any nested page or layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.71,
          "end": 129.81,
          "en": "Therefore, you could of course also add this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.81,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "on the root level of your application to catch any error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 136.233,
          "en": "that's cost anywhere in any of your pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.37,
          "end": 140.133,
          "en": "Again, you can be as granular as needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.105,
          "end": 142.44,
          "en": "Here, I'll go down one level",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.44,
          "end": 145.8,
          "en": "so that I don't replace the entire site",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.8,
          "end": 147.48,
          "en": "with my error screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 147.48,
          "end": 150.63,
          "en": "but instead only a part of that site.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.63,
          "end": 155.63,
          "en": "And here, I'll then simply output some main element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 158.91,
          "en": "with a class name of error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 158.91,
          "end": 161.923,
          "en": "and I'm setting this class name like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 161.923,
          "end": 164.505,
          "en": "because that's not actually a class I prepared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 164.505,
          "end": 165.70499999999998,
          "en": "in this global CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.54500000000002,
          "end": 168.113,
          "en": "which was part of the starting project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 169.484,
          "end": 173.089,
          "en": "And we're importing that globally, not as a CSS module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.089,
          "end": 175.305,
          "en": "They offer those classes from that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.305,
          "end": 177.45,
          "en": "can be used just like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.45,
          "end": 179.31,
          "en": "And then here I'll add a H1 element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 179.31,
          "end": 183.39,
          "en": "where I say an error occurred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 185.733,
          "en": "and then maybe some details about that error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.02,
          "end": 189.72,
          "en": "And for that to learn more about this error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.72,
          "end": 192.09,
          "en": "we can actually use some props here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 192.09,
          "end": 196.11,
          "en": "in this error page component because when setting up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.11,
          "end": 198.813,
          "en": "such a component in such a error or JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.785,
          "end": 202.86,
          "en": "NextJS will pass some props to that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.86,
          "end": 206.19,
          "en": "Most importantly, it will provide an error prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 206.19,
          "end": 209.193,
          "en": "which can contain more details about the error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.24,
          "end": 212.19,
          "en": "Now, the actual error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 212.19,
          "end": 214.86,
          "en": "will actually be hidden by NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.86,
          "end": 218.73,
          "en": "so that you can't accidentally expose any information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.73,
          "end": 222.39,
          "en": "that shouldn't be exposed to your end users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.39,
          "end": 224.52,
          "en": "But if your error would be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.52,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "that also contains some error code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 227.88,
          "en": "or anything like that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 227.88,
          "end": 230.1,
          "en": "you could use that here in this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 230.1,
          "end": 233.52,
          "en": "to show a more fine tuned error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 233.52,
          "end": 235.98,
          "en": "Here, I'll simply output a generic message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.98,
          "end": 240.51,
          "en": "and say, failed to fetch meal data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.51,
          "end": 243.153,
          "en": "Please try again later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.34,
          "end": 247.44,
          "en": "Now, if you add that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 247.44,
          "end": 251.01,
          "en": "and you reload this meals page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 251.01,
          "end": 252.96,
          "en": "you'll get something strange here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.96,
          "end": 254.97,
          "en": "You'll get another error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.97,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "where we learn that error.JS must be a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 261.243,
          "en": "And indeed that's the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.473,
          "end": 266.01,
          "en": "This error component that's stored in an error.JS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.01,
          "end": 268.2,
          "en": "must be a client component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.2,
          "end": 271.44,
          "en": "simply because NextJS basically ensures",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.44,
          "end": 274.95,
          "en": "that you can catch any errors with that component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 274.95,
          "end": 278.19,
          "en": "including errors that happen on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.19,
          "end": 281.973,
          "en": "so after the pages were rendered on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.93,
          "end": 286.68,
          "en": "That's why this directive must be added here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 286.68,
          "end": 290.07,
          "en": "And with it added, you see that this goes away.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 290.07,
          "end": 293.79,
          "en": "If we now reload, we'll of course still get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 293.79,
          "end": 296.853,
          "en": "but now we get our custom error page here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 297.75,
          "end": 300.84,
          "en": "which you of course now could fine tune if you wanted to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 300.84,
          "end": 305.84,
          "en": "but here I'll go with that and that's how we can therefore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.153,
          "end": 307.553,
          "en": "now handle errors like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 308.553,
          "end": 310.74,
          "en": "With that, of course, I'll go back to that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 310.74,
          "end": 313.23,
          "en": "meals.js file in the lib folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 313.23,
          "end": 315.72,
          "en": "and comment out that line of code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 315.72,
          "end": 317.673,
          "en": "because I don't wanna throw an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 318.513,
          "end": 321.113,
          "en": "I just wanted to show you how you could handle them.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
